<title>GREECE: Greek Natl Bank ups 96 net, cuts loan rate.</title>
<headline>Greek Natl Bank ups 96 net, cuts loan rate.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State National Bank of Greece said its fiscal 1996 profits before taxes and provisions rose 14.2 percent to 61.4 billion drachmas from 53.8 billion a year earlier.</p>
<p>National Bank's president Theodore Karatzas told a press conference the bank would cut its base lending rate by 100 basis points to 15.5 percent effective February 24.</p>
<p>Also, savings deposit rates will come down by 50 basis points to 9.50 percent, he said.</p>
<p>National will also lower rates on its adjustable mortgages by 75 basis points to 14.0 percent.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
